---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/about.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="wArcxs — about" description="wArcxs is a boutique studio focused on Minecraft client systems, modular builds and compatibility — worked on directly by the people who make them.">
  <div class="ab">
    <nav class="ab-nav">
      <a href="/" class="ab-mark-link" aria-label="wArcxs — home"><span class="ab-mark">About</span></a>
      <ul class="ab-links">
        <li><a href="/services">compatibility</a></li>
        <li><a href="/products/lockmaster">client</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">contact</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <header class="ab-hero">
      <h1>wArcxs is a client engineering studio.<br>We build around Minecraft — end to end.</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="ab-sec">
      <p class="ab-lead">You work directly with the people shaping the client — from module behavior and configs to the build that actually ships.</p>
      <p class="ab-body">We keep the loop tight. A small number of builds at a time means faster decisions, cleaner configs and a team that understands the checks, flags and version constraints around the product.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="ab-sec ab-cols">
      <div class="ab-col">
        <h2 class="ab-h">how we test</h2>
        <p>We start with the target version and environment, then tune modules, profiles and release builds around observed behavior. Compatibility is treated as something to verify, not something to promise forever.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ab-col">
        <h2 class="ab-h">what we build</h2>
        <p>Client-side systems, module interfaces, config layers and release tooling. We also build the protection, licensing and infrastructure that keeps those builds organized as versions change.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="ab-sec ab-contact">
      <p class="ab-eyebrow">have a build in mind?</p>
      <a class="ab-email" href="mailto:hello@warcxs.com">hello@warcxs.com</a>
      <p class="ab-loc">Spain based &mdash; working worldwide.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="ab-foot"><span>2026 wArcxs &mdash; &copy; All rights reserved</span></footer>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
